  i A query that returns many documents uses a lot of bandwidth, makes mutations more likely to conflict, and fails once it reaches the Convex query limits.
  
  i Use .take() to load only the first few documents, or .paginate() to load them one page at a time. If this query always returns a small number of documents, suppress this diagnostic with a biome-ignore comment.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

